{"text": ". 5\nLEO BURNETT U.S.A. i\nADVERTISING\n\nPRUDENTIAL PLAZA + CHICAGO, ILLINOIS 60601 - 312-565-5959\n\nos TYVED\u2122 dure 17, 1981\nBECEIVED\nMr, dames Thompson wee\n\nPHILIP NORRIS U.S.A. 48 198h\n100 Park Avenue cup BS\n\nNew York NY 10017 CLAUDE BECK\n\nDear Jim:\n\nThis is in response to our conversation yesterday regarding the various ways we\nmonitor magazine performance. Also, attached at your request is the current\nme contract.\n\nMagazines are monitored on the following bases:\n\nCirculation: ABC Publishers\u2019 Statements and Audits are used to monitor\ncirculation delivery and acquisition.\n\nPublishers\u2019 Statements of Ownership are used to evaluate\ncirculation vitality - e.g., newsstand sales, rate, print\norders, etc.\n\nSeparation: Lynch Transcript is used to monitor separation performance,\n\nPositioning: In addition to Lynch, the major magazines are required to pro-\nvide quarterly analyses of positioning by quarter of the maga-\nzine for Philip Morris and the competition.\n\nAdvertising\nPages: PIB, MNI and Ad Age are used to m\npages placed in each magazine uti\n\nitor the total advertising\nized by Philip Morris.\n\nAd/Edit\nRatios: Hall Reports are used to monitor status and change in adver-\ntising-to-editorial ratios.\n\nIn addition to these monitoring techniques - and our work with the Publisher's\nStatement of Ownership is probably unique - we maintain regular, continuing con~\ntact with each and every magazine through their representatives and management.\n\nBest regards,\nLEO BURNETT U.S.A.\n\nbev\n\n(gif Robert G. Houghtlin, Jr.\nVice Presi\n\nlent.\nce: Mr. Claude Beck - PuCoY Resoctate fava Director\n\nzs0s490%0z", "words": [{"text": ".", "x0": 383, "y0": 116, "x1": 385, "y1": 118, "conf": 26.0}, {"text": "5", "x0": 641, "y0": 98, "x1": 664, "y1": 114, "conf": 29.0}, {"text": "LEO", "x0": 281, "y0": 116, "x1": 318, "y1": 129, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "BURNETT", "x0": 330, "y0": 116, "x1": 426, "y1": 129, "conf": 95.0}, {